From 45226e02554c1dbf87a8e4d4c59537355f38c367 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 03:25:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Icon packs find more apps; Watch Next keeps up with what you
 watch

Icon packs:
- Every way of finding an app's drawing is tried in turn, and a drawing the pack lists but
  can't load no longer stops the search; drawings are looked for in mipmap as well as
  drawable, written plain or as @drawable/name.png, and loaded with the pack's own theme,
  which some packs (Material You styles) need.
- An app is also looked up by the app's own name as well as its TV screen's name, without
  TV parts in its package name (com.example.tv), and through the same maker's other entries
  when the drawing's name fits (com.hulu.livingroomplus through com.hulu.plus).
- Choose from the icon pack now says what TunaHome picked by itself, with the app's package,
  or that it found nothing, so a missing icon can be told apart from a wrong one.

Watch Next:
- The row follows the TV's list as it changes: apps save where you got to as you leave them,
  often a few seconds after the home screen is back, which the row missed for five minutes.
  It also looks once more 15 seconds after you come back.
- An entry an app changes in place (the next game, the next episode, a new picture under the
  same address) now shows the change, instead of counting as the same.
- A change that came in while the last look was still fetching pictures is no longer dropped.

